e). Photograph of the street front and the 21st Street flank from the north-east, taken with the camera square to the front; unknown photographer, undated (people on the walk and the stoop). Reproduced on chicagology.com, Prairie Avenue, 2100 S. Prairie. A print of the same view is J. W. Taylor's, 'Sherman, John B., Residence', Art Institute of Chicago, Ryerson & Burnham Archives (mqc 29581).","source_id":"chicagology_2100_sherman_photo","tier":1,"tier_label":"period/eyewitness","url":"https://chicagology.com/chicagostreets/prairieavenue/2100prairie/","what_it_does_not_supply":["colour: the print is monochrome","a date: undated","the south flank, the rear and the 21st Street flank's far half"],"what_it_supplies":["the street front's composition: the library pavilion, the porch and balcony, the parlour and the corner oriel","the storeys: the high basement, the two storeys, the mansard's attic and the pavilion's gable","the roof: the mansard's faces, the dormers, the pavilion's gable, the corner pyramid and the great stack","the 21st Street flank's nearer half, the stoop's two flights and the iron fence"]},"uses":["other_scene"]}
